A||||86||TheFiero64||All read, Update on Anthony's condition||||4||
Z||000000||TheFiero64||01-07-2001||10:49 AM||||I will keep all updates I get from chahn72 in this thread. He got our flowers.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by chahn72:<BR><B>The man in the Fiero is Anthony Barber.  He received your flowers today, and let me say that we are so overwhelmed by your support.  Words cannot express what your gift has done for us and his family.<P>I'm not sure how much you all have read, but let me let you know who I am and my connection to Anthony.<P>My name is Chip, and my sister Abby is Anthony's girlfriend.  She was driving the Toyota Turcel that was in front of Anthony.  The Turcel is also totaled, though not nearly as badly as the Fiero.  Abby was released from the hospital the same day as the accident.  She's a little sore, and they're still keeping tabs on her to make sure, but her injuries are the type that only time will heal.<P>Anthony suffered a broken femur and two contusions on his brain.  He had surgery on his leg yesterday(they fixed his nose the at the same time).  Surgery went very well.  The surgeon indicated that the break was very clean, and he could probably put weight on it almost immediately.  He is out of intensive care, and has been upgraded to serious/stable condition, and is now in progressive care.  He is sometimes awake, and aware.  He recognizes people and is talking (sometimes not making sense).  <P>Tonight I am told he was actually sitting up and feeding himself.  <P>The road to recovery will be a long one, but easier because of the support we have seen from people such as yourselves.<P>If there is an administrator of this forum, please send me an email address if you're interested in ongoing updates.<P>Once again, both of our families thank you for your kindness in this horrible time.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||4
Z||000001||87GT||01-07-2001||11:14 AM||||It sure is nice to know that Pennocks Fiero Forum made a big impression to Anthony, his family, and his friends.  Im really glad to hear that Anthony is doing so much better. <BR>:-)||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||01-07-2001||02:53 PM||||I second that..thats really cool! Cliff needs to read this.||||reg||14
Z||000003||BAM-BAM||01-07-2001||03:16 PM||||  What are we as a Forum doing for Anthony? Might I suggest that we each send $10.00 to he and his family to offset the medical expenses and help him afford a new Fiero when he gets better? Better yet, why don't we as a Forum do this for the guy. There is an 88 Coupe for sale on YAHOO that comes with a 3800 Series II engine, the guy is only ashking $1000.00 for both. We could get donations from forum members and buy this set up and have it ready for him when he recovers. That's a small price for such a large guesture that could very well bring pennocks some national attention. I say let's do it. We will contact Mike Valentine (Mr. Fiero) and see if he would be willing to take the donations, buy the car, and then have some assistance from some Forum members (myself included) to swap the 4Cyl Out with the 3800. I'm in!!!!  <A HREF="http://www.webflight.org/fieros/88_coupe.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.webflight.org/fieros/88_coupe.html</A> <P> Peace, B2 OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach/KYB Susp.<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats,headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Gauges And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH<p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 01-07-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000004||Stoic||01-07-2001||03:38 PM||||Glad to hear that he's doing better.  It's great to see the responce from people here after something like this happens.  If this idea of donating a car to him gets going, I'd be glad to help out.<P>------------------<BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||01-07-2001||04:01 PM||||I am glad he is doing better!<BR>If we as a forum are going to get him a car, I think it would be better to get an original car. Maybe a nice GT. There are a few of them in the mall section. That way we don't have to "build it up" just go over it so he has no problems.(brakes,tune-up,exhaust,suspension,etc) Even though the 88 with the 3800 engine sounds nice I don't think it comes with everything to install it. (adapters and such, The little things that always get ya) The labor part of it may be more involved too. I think a car with low miles and in excellent shape would be more practical.||||reg||14
Z||000006||mrfiero||01-07-2001||04:29 PM||||I'd be more than happy to help out.  If we could narrow down what kind of Fiero (year, model, etc.) it would help.  <P>I think taking donations to offset any medical expenses should be the first concern (unless his insurance will cover everything).<P>The next thing we should figure out is how much each person should contribute.......should we have a set dollar amount or just send what you are comfortable with and can afford?<P>E-mail me and/or post your suggestions and we can start planning on what to do.   ||||reg||1
Z||000007||87ECO5||01-07-2001||08:51 PM||||<B>FieroWife</B> and I are definitely in on this one!  Just let us know when and where to send the money.<P>Interesting ... I just got this in my mail from <B>2M4 Dale</B>:<BR><I><BR>From: "Alan & Becky Wallace" &lt;wallace@erinet.com&gt;<BR>To: &lt;fiero-list@fiero.org&gt;<BR>Cc: &lt;wallace@erinet.com&gt;<BR>Sent: Saturday, January 06, 2001 12:09 PM<BR>Subject: (Fiero) For Sale: '86 Fiero GT<P>Gang,<P>Hate to hit you up with a For Sale ad, but here goes...<P>This car must be sold this coming week (by 12 Jan 2001) or will be donated to charity or traded in to a dealer.  I am HIGHLY MOTIVATED and will accept the 1ST REASONABLE (preferably cash) OFFER.  Car is located in SW Ohio.  Feel free to pass this message on to any interested parties:<P>'86 Fiero GT, all original, V6/4-spd, 101K miles, loaded, black with gray interior, brand new Ocelot performance exhaust, new shocks/struts/brakes, interior very good condition, exterior paint faded, AM/FM cassette with new speakers all around.  Car is good and strong.<P>Please contact me at wallace@erinet.com.  This car is too good to go to a dealer.  Reason for sale:  I have too many cars and am buying yet another.  So, this one has to go!<P>Warm Regards,<P>Al Wallace                         wallace@erinet.com<BR></I><P>I say this is interesting because he mentions sending it to charity if he can't sell it.  Maybe we could get this gentleman to "donate" and car to Anthony and we could raise enough money to have it painted.<P>Just a thought ...<p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 01-07-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000008||Cheever2||01-07-2001||10:11 PM||||Yo! I'm in. <BR>It's not like I have money sitting around, but each doing our part wouldn't hurt any of us.  And it's definitely a good cause.<P>I agree if a car is given, it should be stock.  There are plenty of Forum members who have cars for sale.  The benefit of it coming from one of our own is that we can all just send our portion of the funds directly to him/her.  There would be no middleman.  Also it would be a quicker transaction (although I guess Mr. Barber isn't getting back on the horse anytime soon, huh?).<BR>The question now is: who has a decent car for sale, with an unpredictable price tag?<BR><P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I>||||reg||6
Z||000009||BAM-BAM||01-07-2001||11:17 PM||||  Ok, I conceed to the stock Fiero gift. It does make better sense. I was just in a hurry to get the ball rolling and that was the first thing that came to mind (resent research). I'm down with whatever the majority decides. I also believe that it would be awesome for as many of us to be there to represent when the gift is handed over. I enjoy special gestures like this and am willing to do what ever I can. Lets make a decision on how much to donate and what to buy, and when to give it. I'M IN!!!!!<P> Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
