Z||000033||mrfiero||01-08-2001||08:37 PM||||Hey everone......I just got back from delivering a Fiero to Paul Herder in Kansas.<P>It looks like we have a lot of interest in this.  Maybe Wayne (wkayl)and I could do this together, since we are both in the area.<P>I like Cliffs idea about the list of donators......anything to keep it all in check is fine with me.<P>I don't see a problem setting up a checking or special banking account for this.  E-mail me with what you find out Wayne.<P>As for what Fiero.......I know of a nice 35K mile '85 GT for $5000.  It wouldn't need any work at all and is bone stock.  The good news is it is local, so no lost time/$$ retrieving one from out of state.<P>Once we can set up a fund or account somewhere we can start!  ||||reg||10
Z||000034||wkayl||01-08-2001||09:01 PM||||Here is what I found out.  My bank will set up an account in my name.  It will be set up with the banks address with Anthony in the first line so all checks will be mailed directly to the bank and deposited.  I will have the account number if anyone wants to do an electronic deposit.  The dispersment of funds would be by me writing a check.  Details will be worked out with Anthony or his family as to where funds will go  (with discussion in the forum of course).  I was thinking that when the account is closed (we will have to figure out a time limit) I would scan the deposit statements blocking out the names of depositors and posting on a webpage for everyone to be able to view.  The reason for that is so everyone knows this is all above board.  The account is a no interest one so I would have no tax problems.  Please let me know if anyone else has suggestions.||||reg||1
Z||000035||mrfiero||01-08-2001||09:10 PM||||That sounds good Wayne.  I say go ahead and set it up so we can get the ball rolling.  This will be a good gesture, regardless if he decides to buy another Fiero or not. <P>Here is an e-mail I got from Chip updating Anthony's condition:<P><BR>--------- Forwarded message ----------<BR>From: "W. Hahn" <BR>To: mrfiero@juno.com<BR>Date: Sun, 7 Jan 2001 23:27:11 -0700<BR>Subject: update on anthony<P><BR>good evening. just wanted to get you an update.<P>Today, Anthony had some scans done to check for internal bleeding,<BR>because<BR>of a low blood count. Turns out thankfully, there was no bleeding found,<BR>and the low count is likely due to the surgery on friday(for the leg),<BR>and/or poor nutrition(he hasn't eaten since tuesday).<P>Tonight, he had dinner--some broth, tea and juice. He perked up a bit,<BR>and<BR>when I left the hospital, he was fairly tired, and was watching some tv.<BR>He's still in and out, and I think while we've passed a major milestone,<BR>the<BR>hard part is ahead of us, while we wait and see the extent of the brain<BR>injury, and how long the recovery process will be.<P>I told Anthony about your gift, and who it came from, and the level of<BR>support that is coming from this forum. He really brightened at this,<BR>and<BR>he says "thank you". I also passed along some of your notes of support<BR>to<BR>his parents and they are so thankful.<P>I also want to express my gratitude for your support. I have seen<BR>firsthand<BR>its effects, and it has truly lifted spirits.<P>More to come....<P>Chip<P>||||reg||10
Z||000036||Oreif||01-08-2001||09:22 PM||||Go ahead and set it up. Just post the address and info required and I'll get a check going.||||reg||14
Z||000037||sqoach||01-08-2001||09:23 PM||||never thought to look at this thread until i noticed that quite a few members have responded. i saw that picture of that wrecked fiero...it was bad. i can't believe that he (anthony) is still alive. but that's good news. i would definately like to help out here.<BR>but, old lar has a very good point. what if he doesn't want another fiero? i know someone in town that had a fiero, wrecked the engine, and didn't care to get another one. talking to the family would be a good idea. and, if he does want another fiero, i think we should try to get one that was close to what he had, a fastback gt. that 85 gt sounds nice though.<BR>just some thoughts.<P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig_2.JPG"> ||||reg||10
Z||000038||tgowens||01-08-2001||10:41 PM||||count me in -- i'll contribute somehow - and - if the new Fiero needs a part or two, let me know -- I'm sure that between mrfiero and the Fiero Shop here we can completely restore a Fiero for Anthony.<P>I am saddened by the loss that the families have experienced, It is a terrible tragedy when there is a loss of life in a situation like this. <P>I didn't know any of these people but I feel sadness anytime something like this happens. My heart goes out to those affected and they are in my prayers.||||reg||1
Z||000039||Seanh||01-08-2001||10:51 PM||||Guess I should have checked this tread sooner. Count my donation in also, Happy to help out a fellow owner. I am also fairly close (Less then a 4 hour drive, 3 if I take the Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) and would be willing to come out and help if you need it, if it be working on a car to get ready for him, or presenting it, contact me. If he indeed wants another Fiero, then I think that would be the best course of action. That was a nasty wreck, and that Fiero probally saved his life, I would think thats reason enough to want another one, but thats just me. Let me know whats going to happen and dont hesitate to ask for help if you need it, be nice to get out to Denver one of these days.||||reg||1
Z||000040||FieroLisa||01-08-2001||11:21 PM||||I don't have too much cash to spare, but I wouldn't mind helping a little bit. Whenever more info is given about where to do deposits etc just post a new forum post so it's easier to check!<P><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR>*As Always, Updated Website*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/</A>||||reg||1
