Z||000044||mrfiero||01-09-2001||12:20 AM||||OK.....we have a few problems to iron out first.  I just got another e-mail from Chip and it looks like he will be unable to relay any more updates (at the request of Anthony's attorney).  I guess in our haste we forgot about the pending litigation that will likely ensue.<P>We need to find out if Anthony wants another Fiero or if we should just donate to the fund his family has already set-up.  <P>Here's Chip's latest e-mail:<P>On Mon, 8 Jan 2001 21:03:57 -0700 "W. Hahn" &lt;chiph@qwest.net&gt; writes:<BR>&gt; Hi. I wanted to touch base with you. First of all, I need to say <BR>&gt; that I'm<BR>&gt; not going to be able to provide specifics anymore, at the advice of <BR>&gt; our<BR>&gt; attorney. I will say that spirits are high, and we are all <BR>&gt; encouraged. I<BR>&gt; am also encouraged by what I have read on the website, and the <BR>&gt; eagerness to<BR>&gt; help. There are indeed some costs associated with this incident <BR>&gt; that we are<BR>&gt; asking help with, and we have set up a fund for this purpose.<BR>&gt; <BR>&gt; Donations will gratefully be accepted at:<BR>&gt; <BR>&gt; The Anthony S. Barber Fund<BR>&gt; C/O Minnequa Bank<BR>&gt; 154 S. McCullough Blvd.<BR>&gt; Pueblo West, CO 81007<BR>&gt; <BR>&gt; Any assistance will be appreciated, and will go a long way to <BR>&gt; helping the<BR>&gt; family focus on Anthony, and his recovery.<BR>&gt; <BR>&gt; Chip<P><BR>That sums it up pretty well.  We could either send in our donations individually or have one of us collect it and make one big donation in the name of Pennock's Fiero Forum.<P>We could also do both too.  We could donate to this fund AND buy another Fiero.  From the pictures of the wreck it looks like he had an '87 base coupe (I'll find out exactly what it was), so we could buy a nice '87 base coupe for less than $1000 and still be able to help him financially with the hospital/rehab bills that will start racking up.<P>LMK what you all think......let's get a consensus. ||||reg||4
Z||000045||sqoach||01-09-2001||12:42 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sqoach:<BR><B> and, if he does want another fiero, i think we should try to get one that was close to what he had, a fastback gt. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>ok, so i was wrong about the model.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR>i saw another picture on the first thread, and it appears to be a 87 or 88 coupe. that picture scared the heck outta me when i saw it. i still can't believe he survived. i am glad to hear he is doing better.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000046||Cheever2||01-09-2001||12:59 AM||||I want to stick with the original idea (the car from our group), and individually donate directly to the family's fund.  In our individual donations, we will surely mention the Forum.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000047||mrfiero||01-09-2001||02:29 AM||||I e-mailed Chip to find out if Anthony even wants another Fiero.  The answer to that question will determine how we should proceed.<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000048||wkayl||01-09-2001||06:29 AM||||I e-mailed hip also.  The following is what I sent:<P>I am the one that brought Anthony's accident to our Forum.  I am off work this coming Thursday, Jan 11th.  I was wondering if it would be possible for me to meet with Anthony's family at the hospital sometime during the day before 2PM.  I have been checking into setting up an account at my bank for donations from the forum members and would like to make sure it is ok with them before I continue.  If you could check with their family on a meeting time for us, I would appreciate it.<P><BR>I received a response similar to Mrfiero.  (Mike, let me know if you are available Thursday.  I could swing by and pick you up.) I will hold off on starting an account untill we find out more, but a lump summ from the Forum would be nice.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000049||Seanh||01-09-2001||05:34 PM||||I think we should make the donation in one lump sum from PFF as a whole. But, If he indeed wants another Fiero, I think we should select one person to send our donations to, and once he has enough money, we should purchase a nice Fiero, yet low-priced, and fix it up for him, and if there is any money left over, donate that to their fund. I think people should also feel free to donate any parts that might be needed to get the car in good shape.||||reg||1
Z||000050||mrfiero||01-09-2001||06:04 PM||||I suppose Anthony or his family could always sell the Fiero if they/he didn't want it.  It would still be a good gesture.<P>I have a storage yard, so I can store whatever vehicle is purchased.  I have tons of spare parts , so I can help out there too.  I also know where I can get a nice lower mileage (around 85K miles) '88 4-cyl. engine.  If we could buy that $600 '88 coupe on Yahoo and install this motor and fix whatever else is wrong with it we should come away with less than $1500 spent......any excess money would then be donated to his fund.  <P>Wayne......I can be available on Thursday.  LMK when to be ready.<p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 01-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000051||jerpro||01-09-2001||06:09 PM||||this is just an Idea...<BR>Could anyone mass produce some sort of sticker (good looking) that we could put on our fieros for donating money to the pff forum donation account?<BR>This would show nationwide that we as fiero owners care for other owners that we have never meet, and would bring back the reputation to our cars.<BR>Or someone could put the stickers for sale and use the money for the fund...<BR>something like that.<BR>just throwing ideas in mid air, you guys tell me what you think.<BR>||||reg||1
