Z||000056||Cliff Pennock||01-09-2001||10:13 PM||||Ok, I've made a concept text for the webpage. I need someone to turn it into a better text than it is since english is not my native language...<P><I><B>On January 2nd 2001, a 16 year old Lakewood High School sophomore was driving in a Chevy Suburban between 70 and 90 miles an hour down the dotted line, trying to pass between two cars. This caused a 5-car  accident which killed 57-year-old Eugene Martinelli and seriously injured 21-year-old Anthony Barber driving his Fiero.<P>As fellow Fiero owners, we would like to show our support to Anthony and his family.<P>This does not mean that we think Eugene's death isn't as equally devestating for his friends and family. Our thoughts and prayers go out to them. These are difficult times for both families but as a group we have chosen to help someone to whom we, here at Pennock's Fiero Forum, can relate so well.<P>We sincerely hope other people will do something similar for the Martelli family.<P>It started when wkayl on PFF attended us to this news story. Then the idea to help the family started with a simple gesture, a Get Well Bouquet send by TheFiero64 in name of all the people on PFF. This simple gesture alone provided enormous support for Anthony. Next, Gold-86SE came with the idea we should all donate towards a new Fiero for him. And that got the ball rolling.<P>This page is for everyone that would like to make a donation. It's totally up to you how much you would like to donate. Be it $5 or $50, everything helps. The amount you donate will be kept confidential and will only be known to me and the person that will collect the money.<P>Please fill in your real name and if applicable your PFF screenname below as well as a valid email adress I can use to verify your intent. When everything has been ironed out you will receive an email how the donation should be made.<P>In name of all members of PFF, I sincerely thank you for your help. It shows people do care.</B></I><P>Also, don't forget to help TheFiero64 with a dollar or so for the bouquet he had send. I'm sure that if he receives more than he paid for the flowers, he will put it back in the fund.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000057||Jaygee79||01-09-2001||10:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever2:<BR><B>TheFiero64 probably wouldn't say it himself, but he didn't get much help with the flowers.  A buck (and 34 cents for stamp) wouldn't hurt anybody.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You're right, he won't say anything.  So far only 2 people have helped out.  If anyone needs an address to send any donations for the flowers to, email me or TheFiero64.||||reg||1
