Z||000070||stimpy||01-10-2001||02:55 PM||||Someone may have already volunteered the editing, but do to my WebTV handicap, this page ends for me a couple of posts down. So here is my editorial undertaking...<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<P><BR><I><B>On January 2nd, 2001, a 16 year old Lakewood High School sophomore was driving in a Chevy Suburban between 70 and 90 miles an hour down the center line of the road, attempting to pass between two cars. This caused a 5-car  accident which killed 57-year-old Eugene Martinelli and seriously injured 21-year-old Anthony Barber driving his Fiero.<P>As fellow Fiero owners, we would like to show our support to Anthony and his family.<P>This does not mean that we think Eugene's death isn't as equally devestating for his friends and family. Our thoughts and prayers go out to them. These are difficult times for both families but as a group we have chosen to help someone to whom we here at Pennock's Fiero Forum can relate to well.<P>We sincerely hope other people will do something similar for the Martelli family.<P>It started when wkayl on PFF alerted us to this news story. Then the idea to help the family started with a simple gesture, a Get Well Bouquet sent by TheFiero64 in name of all the people on PFF. This simple gesture alone provided enormous support for Anthony. Next, Gold-86SE came with the idea we should all donate towards a new Fiero for him. And that got the ball rolling.<P>This page is for everyone that would like to make a donation. It's totally up to you how much you would like to donate. Be it $5 or $50, everything helps. The amount you donate will be kept confidential and will only be known to me and the person that will collect the money.<P>Please fill in your real name and if applicable your PFF screenname below as well as a valid email address that I will use to verify your intent. When everything has been ironed out you will receive an email describing how the donation should be made.<P>In name of all members of PFF, I sincerely thank you for your help. It shows people do care.</B></I><BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Boy, am I glad I didn't have to translate that back into Dutch!<BR>Anyhow, this is the type of gesture that makes me proud to be part of a group like this. I look forward to participating.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000071||TheFiero64||01-10-2001||06:20 PM||||That is a great job cliff. <P>------------------<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||14
Z||000072||wkayl||01-10-2001||08:10 PM||||Here is an update on the account for Anthony.  As per comments in e-mail from Chip, I have decided to act with no contact or input from them.  This way we will have no affect on any legal actions they may or may not pursue.   I am going to my bank tomorrow morning to set up an account and will post the information ASAP after that.  I will wait to be contacted by him or his family as to the dispersment of funds. If anyone has comments, please feel free to voice your opinions.||||reg||1
