Z||000075||Seanh||01-10-2001||11:25 PM||||Well, I cant say I'm really suprised by the turn out of this group in response to this thread, I knew how great this group was since I started reading it. Its really nice to see how willing you are to help out people we dont even know. I think the text Cliff posted sounds great. I think we should go the route of getting him another Fiero and donating the rest of the money to his fund. I think there will be quite a bit left over, judging from the response from the group. I was thinking, but then I thought there would be to much trouble comming with it, but, maybe we should start a donation fund for PFF. Taking donations all the time, and using them in situations like these. Just an off the top idea I had, but sounds like a good one to me!? Like I said before, if you guys would need/like any help working on the car, drop me a line, I could make it out there in 4 hours.||||reg||14
Z||000076||Cheever2||01-10-2001||11:36 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Seanh:<BR><B>a donation fund for PFF. Taking donations all the time, and using them in situations like these.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Interesting idea.  What if the people who make a monthly contribution <I>of any size</I> would get a break on something... what, I don't know.  Just thinking on the run here.  But that would be motivation to make regular donations.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000077||wkayl||01-11-2001||12:11 AM||||Good news everyone.  I recieved an e-mail saying Anthony's family will meet with me at the hospital tomorrow (11th).  This will be a birthday I won't forget.  I have asked Mrfiero if he would like to ride along.  The bank visit will be put on hold untill I get back from Denver.  More updates tomorrow evening.||||reg||1
Z||000078||Cliff Pennock||01-11-2001||06:33 AM||||That's great wkayl! Keep us updated.||||reg||1
Z||000079||zeusrekning||01-11-2001||07:57 AM||||Reading this thread makes me very proud to be part of this community. I think if everyone would imagine themselves in anthony's position then haveing a group like us (does he even know how big the fieo "thing" is on the internet?) do this for you.  I think it is something he would never forget. And he'll probably be a fiero fanatic forever. ||||reg||1
Z||000080||Oreif||01-11-2001||10:43 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Phil:<BR><B>All this is well and good but I have one question, does this family need or even want assistance? I would imagine there are going to be big insurance settlements to come.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think this idea of donating money and/or getting a replacement Fiero is a great thing. <BR>One reason is that most of the insurance settlements/lawsuits he and his family may or may not get will take time. There will possibly be a lot of litigation and court dates. Had a friend who got hit by a car while he was on his motorcycle, (he was sitting on it in his driveway when a guy playing with his stereo drove off the road and hit him.) He spent almost 3 months in the hospital and 3 months in physical theropy. By the time the insurance and lawsuits were settled, almost 5 years had past. I am not saying it would take the same amount of time, But we all know how "litigation" works.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>(5 Years without a Fiero?!?!, I'd go crazy!)<P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 01-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000081||wkayl||01-11-2001||06:58 PM||||Hello everyone.<P>Mrfiero and I had the opportunity to visit with Anthony’s parents today.  We visited with his dad for almost an hour, his mom joining us the last 15 minutes.  They couldn’t say enough nice things about the folks here on the Forum.  The first flowers to arrive in his room were from us.  His dad said he perked up considerably when he heard whom they were from.  His dad read the card on the flowers.  It said “from the Fiero Gang”.   He asked him when he joined a “gang”?  <P>The Fiero he was driving was an 84.  They have owned it since 1990.  His dad used to drive a Fiero also but now drives an (can I say it?) MR2.  We had to rib him about that.  <P>As far as visiting with Anthony, he was resting while we were there and didn’t get a chance.  We told his parents we would stop back in a week or so.  He will be transferring to a different hospital in a few days.  His dad says he looks remarkable considering the condition of his car.  Contrary to news reports, he was wearing his seat belt.<P>Now the good stuff.  I opened an account today for donations.  Here is where to send them;<P>1st Bank of Northern Colorado<BR>Anthony Barber Benefit<BR>% Wayne Kayl<BR>1352 West Eisenhower Boulevard<BR>Loveland, CO 80539<P>Make the checks payable to;<P>1st Bank/Wayne Kayl<P>with    “Anthony Barber Benefit “  in the memo line.<P>If any electronic transfers are needed, check with your bank as to the procedure.  E-mail me if you have any questions at wkayl717@aol.com<P>I have deposited some money to activate the account.  The statements I get from the bank will have only the amount of the deposit, not who they were from.  You can send as little or as much as you would like, no one will know.  It is a free account for 1 year.  I will create a web page and scan in the statements each month so everyone can see the progress of deposits and withdraws.  I left it up to his parents as to how and when the money will be released.  <P>Please let me know if you have any questions.  <P>Wayne R Kayl<BR>Loveland, CO<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000082||Oreif||01-11-2001||07:07 PM||||I'll drop a check in the mail first thing in the morning!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000083||BAM-BAM||01-11-2001||07:51 PM||||   I will be contributing this weekend. Good work wkayl!!!!!<BR> <BR>  Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach/KYB Susp.<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats,headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Gauges And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||12
